## Context

Step B of 0978. The 2026-09-28 disposable-HOME probe showed that a broken projected link
makes Claude Code silently drop instructions and hooks while still answering. A
SessionStart hook cannot detect this: it vanishes with the settings it lives in. The check
must therefore run in the shell, before the runtime starts: a wrapper (`claude`, `codex`,
`pi`) that asserts every projected entry resolves to its expected target and refuses to
launch otherwise.

Useful before any move too: it turns 0978's red negative control green and guards today's
existing symlinks (the three private links under `skills/`, `synced/`).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A validator enumerates the expected projections from one declared manifest, not a glob of what happens to exist
- [ ] Shell wrappers for `claude`, `codex` and `pi` run it and exit non-zero with a named culprit on a dangling or foreign link
- [ ] Positive control: a planted broken link in a disposable HOME blocks the launch; negative control: a healthy HOME launches unchanged
- [ ] Bypass is explicit (`IDH_SKIP_VALIDATE=1`) and logged
- [ ] `make check` passes
